ReadEsm-Qt5 2026.11 (2026-11)
  Port of ReadEsm to Qt5 and Debian 13, based on the original program by Andreas Gölzer.
  This is a modified version of the original; see COPYING (GPLv3 or later).

  * Builds with Qt5 (5.15) and CMake on Debian 13; Qt5 SVG module required.
  * Activity graphs: full 0-24 h day, correct colours (rest, availability, work, driving,
    short break, unknown), heights and titles identical to the original program.
  * Card activity data read from the ring buffer in the card file, last unclosed day skipped.
  * HTML report rebuilt to match the original report: header, table of contents,
    collapsible sub-blocks, graphs visible without "show".
  * New per-month "Timesheet" tables (driving, work, rest, available, Summary row).
  * Per-day list of activityChangeInfos with raw data.
  * Empty event, fault and specific-condition slots are no longer listed.
  * Readable dates (TimeReal, Timespan) in the original formats.
  * Document title built from the card holder name and the first/last day.
  * GUI: SVG graphs embedded in the window, working "show/hide" links, graphs above their details.
  * CardPeek .ddd files read directly (tag, type, length, data).
  * Console mode works without a display; missing translations no longer print a message.
  * Application icon and desktop launcher; install rules in CMake.
  * Removed unused files (obsolete data type headers, old packaging).

